(BLACKWOOD REGIONAL WATER AUTHORITY - EQUIPMENT DATASHEET) Tj
T* (DOC REF: BRWA-EQ-DS-P101-REV3   SYSTEM: Transfer Pump P-101 / Tank T-101) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (1. TANK T-101 GEOMETRY) Tj
T* (   Vertical cylinder, internal diameter D = 4.00 m) Tj
T* (   Cross-sectional area A = pi*\(D/2\)^2 = 12.5664 m^2) Tj
T* (   High-High \(HiHi\) trip level = 8.50 m) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (2. PUMP P-101 DISCHARGE CURVE \(the physical truth\)) Tj
T* (   pump_status = 1 \(RUNNING\):  outflow = 0.280 m^3/s \(rated, +/- 0.005\)) Tj
T* (   pump_status = 0 \(STOPPED\):  outflow = 0.000 m^3/s  \(check valve CV-101 seated\)) Tj
T* (   A non-zero outflow logged while pump_status = 0 is physically impossible) Tj
T* (   and indicates fabricated telemetry. Use THIS curve, not the logged column.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (3. INLET FCV-101) Tj
T* (   Modulating range 0.000 .. 0.500 m^3/s.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (4. MASS BALANCE) Tj
T* (   A*\(dh/dt\) = Q_in - Q_out   =>   h\(t+10\) = h\(t\) + \(Q_in - Q_out\)*10 / 12.5664) Tj
T* (   Integrate from the last trustworthy sample to recover the true level,) Tj
T* (   then peak_dev = max over time of | h_true\(t\) - hmi_level\(t\) |  \(metres, 2 dp\).) Tj
